  message: "DONE (already resolved in-code; stale audit premise — no PR). The §17 fail-open containment is already BROAD (any Exception), not OSError-only, at all three worker-execution sites: the analyzer loop (analyze/all_analyzers.py:298 'except Exception as exc' -> record_crashed_pass -> continue) and BOTH linker dispatch paths (linkers/registry.py:802 serial + :843 parallel -> _record_linker_crash -> continue). STRUCTURAL/TEST EVIDENCE: tests/test_orchestrator_fail_open.py injects NON-OSError crashes and asserts containment + partial output — test_crashing_analyzer_does_not_abort_run (raise RuntimeError -> healthy sibling survives, crash recorded pass-level, partial_results_reason set), test_serial_crashing_linker_does_not_abort + test_parallel_crashing_linker_does_not_abort (raise RuntimeError -> contained on both paths), test_crash_recorded_into_limits_when_supplied (raise ValueError -> recorded); plus test_run_behavior_map.py::test_run_behavior_map_emits_partial_json_when_analyzer_crashes. All at 100% coverage (CI gate). WI-libog's 'extend OSError-only to any crash' was already delivered under WI-madal L3."  # 028c
